01:01:49.990 --> 01:01:51.290
Mine looks like four folders.
我的桌面看起来就像四个文件夹。

1448
01:01:51.630 --> 01:01:53.830
Mine is like shit everywhere.
我的桌面到处都是乱七八糟的。

1449
01:01:53.830 --> 01:01:54.490
I know.
我知道。

1450
01:01:57.370 --> 01:02:02.530
Next up in the conference room, Stanley has just purchased a purse.
接下来在会议室里，斯坦利刚刚买了一个手提包。

1451
01:02:02.670 --> 01:02:08.950
And Michael is going to bring Katie an espresso from the machine that is an incentive prize.
迈克尔打算给凯蒂拿一杯咖啡机里的浓缩咖啡，那是作为激励奖品的。

1452
01:02:09.270 --> 01:02:11.350
And Stanley's like, wait a second, Michael.
然后斯坦利说，等等，迈克尔。

1453
01:02:11.710 --> 01:02:14.390
Isn't that meant to be the prize for the top salesman?
那不是应该给销售冠军的奖品吗？

1454
01:02:14.990 --> 01:02:17.170
And Michael's like, it cleans easily.
迈克尔说，这玩意儿很好清理。

1455
01:02:17.590 --> 01:02:18.710
I can clean it.
我可以清理它。

1456
01:02:19.490 --> 01:02:21.070
Now we're going to go to the kitchen.
现在我们要去厨房了。

1457
01:02:21.830 --> 01:02:24.390
Jim enters, asks Dwight for his stapler.
吉姆进来了，向德怀特要他的订书机。

1458
01:02:24.630 --> 01:02:26.110
Dwight says, it's in my purse.
德怀特说，在我的包里。

1459
01:02:26.330 --> 01:02:28.410
Of course, everyone gets a little snicker.
当然，大家都轻笑了一下。

1460
01:02:29.070 --> 01:02:32.450
Well, I just love everyone just slowly looks up and reacts.
我就是喜欢看大家慢慢抬头做出反应的样子。

1461
01:02:32.610 --> 01:02:34.210
But Dwight doesn't even turn around.
但德怀特头都没回。

1462
01:02:34.350 --> 01:02:35.550
He's just digging in the fridge.
他只是在冰箱里翻找着。

1463
01:02:35.750 --> 01:02:36.030
Yes.
没错。

1464
01:02:36.470 --> 01:02:40.070
Again, so much deep background movement back there in the annex.
再说一次，附件办公室背景里的人员走动真是太丰富了。

1465
01:02:40.270 --> 01:02:41.550
Devin is walking around.
德文在走来走去。

1466
01:02:42.050 --> 01:02:44.770
Everybody is in the kitchen or just behind the kitchen.
每个人都在厨房里或者厨房后面。

1467
01:02:44.830 --> 01:02:46.890
Everybody just goes everywhere all at once.
大家一下子全都跑到了各个地方。

1468
01:02:46.890 --> 01:02:47.750
It's so true.
确实如此。

1469
01:02:48.710 --> 01:02:50.870
Now Michael is going to have Pam in his office.
现在迈克尔要把帕姆叫进办公室。

1470
01:02:50.870 --> 01:02:52.410
He's asking about his mail.
他问起他的邮件。

1471
01:02:52.550 --> 01:02:55.870
But what he really wants to know is how girls her age feel about futons.
但他真正想知道的是，她那个年纪的女孩对沙发床怎么看。

1472
01:02:56.170 --> 01:02:57.670
I couldn't get through this scene.
我拍这场戏的时候简直演不下去。

1473
01:02:57.810 --> 01:02:58.950
I mean, how could you?
我是说，怎么可能演得下去？

1474
01:02:59.370 --> 01:03:00.810
It's so ridiculous.
太荒谬了。

1475
01:03:01.210 --> 01:03:02.950
Every time he said futon.
每次他说到沙发床这个词的时候。

1476
01:03:03.690 --> 01:03:06.830
Whatever this relationship is with Katie is just so crazy.
他和凯蒂这段关系真是太疯狂了。

1477
01:03:06.970 --> 01:03:11.690
First of all, it's going to give her a $1,000 coffee maker if she took it.
首先，如果她接受的话，他就要送她一台价值一千美元的咖啡机。

1478
01:03:12.030 --> 01:03:12.210
Yep.
没错。

1479
01:03:12.810 --> 01:03:13.710
Give her a ride home.
还要送她回家。

1480
01:03:14.230 --> 01:03:16.230
I don't know what happens with the futons.
我不知道沙发床那段是怎么回事。

1481
01:03:16.950 --> 01:03:17.250
Yes.
是的。

1482
01:03:17.670 --> 01:03:21.170
Of course, Pam is going to go out and tell Jim all about this conversation.
当然，帕姆出去后会把这段对话全告诉吉姆。

1483
01:03:21.170 --> 01:03:22.950
They're laughing about the futon.
他们正对着沙发床的事笑个不停。

1484
01:03:23.130 --> 01:03:26.650
When Roy comes in, he wants to make up with Pam.
这时罗伊进来了，他想和帕姆和好。

1485
01:03:26.650 --> 01:03:28.690
We talked about this last time.
我们上次讨论过这个。

1486
01:03:28.850 --> 01:03:31.170
He's going to tickle her into forgiving him.
他打算通过挠痒痒来让她原谅他。

1487
01:03:31.530 --> 01:03:32.130
Yes.
是的。

1488
01:03:32.130 --> 01:03:35.330
We discussed my dislike for tickling.
我们讨论过我有多讨厌挠痒痒。

1489
01:03:35.330 --> 01:03:35.930
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1490
01:03:36.310 --> 01:03:44.170
Also, if I were to do what I call a cringe meter for this episode, this one would be a nine on the cringe meter.
另外，如果我要给这一集打个尴尬指数的话，这一段能打到九分。

1491
01:03:44.370 --> 01:03:45.090
This scene?
这一场戏？

1492
01:03:45.170 --> 01:03:45.510
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1493
01:03:45.810 --> 01:03:46.030
Yeah.
是啊。

1494
01:03:46.250 --> 01:03:46.750
Poor Jim.
可怜的吉姆。

1495
01:03:47.090 --> 01:03:47.510
I know.
我知道。

1496
01:03:47.590 --> 01:03:50.610
They're literally almost leaning on him, laughing and tickling.
他们简直就像是靠在他身上又笑又闹地挠痒痒。

1497
01:03:50.830 --> 01:03:51.050
Yeah.
是啊。

1498
01:03:51.290 --> 01:03:52.390
Cringe meter number nine.
尴尬指数九分。

1499
01:03:52.390 --> 01:03:55.230
And then Pam has this talking head that says Jim's a great guy.
然后帕姆对着镜头说吉姆是个好人。

1500
01:03:55.450 --> 01:03:57.190
He's like a brother to her.
他说他就像她的哥哥一样。

1501
01:03:57.350 --> 01:03:58.250
They're best friends.
他们是最好的朋友。

1502
01:03:58.450 --> 01:04:00.410
She really hopes he finds someone.
她真心希望他能找到另一半。

1503
01:04:00.790 --> 01:04:01.050
Wow.
哇。

1504
01:04:01.310 --> 01:04:03.630
Pam, maybe say it enough until you believe it, Pam.
帕姆，也许你得多说几遍直到你自己都信了，帕姆。

1505
01:04:03.690 --> 01:04:03.830
Yeah.
是啊。

1506
01:04:04.030 --> 01:04:04.970
Does she wish?
她真的希望吗？

1507
01:04:05.190 --> 01:04:05.610
Mm-mm.
嗯嗯。

1508
01:04:05.610 --> 01:04:10.610
I don't think so because he's going to find someone in a second and she's not all that happy about it.
我觉得不是，因为他马上就要找到另一半了，而她对此并不怎么高兴。

1509
01:04:10.750 --> 01:04:12.550
She's real sour about it.
她对此感到非常不满。

1510
01:04:13.310 --> 01:04:19.330
Well, Angela's in the conference room and she's looking at purses and we talked a lot about this scene in our original breakdown.
嗯，安吉拉在会议室里看包包，我们在最初的剧本大纲里讨论过很多关于这场戏的内容。

1511
01:04:19.670 --> 01:04:19.970
Yes.
没错。

1512
01:04:20.170 --> 01:04:23.530
All of our dialogue between Angela and Katie is improvising the scene.
安吉拉和凯蒂之间的所有对话都是即兴发挥的。

1513
01:04:23.730 --> 01:04:24.690
We had a lot of fun.
我们玩得很开心。

1514
01:04:25.130 --> 01:04:26.090
You can tell.
看得出来。

1515
01:04:26.290 --> 01:04:26.650
Thank you.
谢谢。

1516
01:04:26.770 --> 01:04:27.830
You guys were good together.
你们俩配合得很好。

1517
01:04:27.990 --> 01:04:28.270
Thank you.
谢谢。

1518
01:04:28.430 --> 01:04:31.350
I actually think there's a spinoff with you, me, and Amy.
我其实觉得可以拍一部关于你、我和艾米的衍生剧。

1519
01:04:32.250 --> 01:04:36.290
Just like an improv show because that scene at the top was so good.
就像即兴表演秀一样，因为开头那场戏太棒了。

1520
01:04:36.610 --> 01:04:40.690
Purse girls, come see us every Thursday night, 9 p.m.
“包包女孩”，每周四晚九点来看我们的演出。

1521
01:04:41.290 --> 01:04:42.470
Oh, that's too late.
噢，那太晚了。

1522
01:04:42.610 --> 01:04:43.030
Too late.
太晚了。

1523
01:04:43.210 --> 01:04:43.410
Sorry.
抱歉。

1524
01:04:43.810 --> 01:04:45.910
It's $35, two drink minimum.
票价35美元，每人至少点两杯饮料。

1525
01:04:46.130 --> 01:04:46.970
There is no parking.
没有停车位。

1526
01:04:47.450 --> 01:04:48.150
Starts at four.
四点开始。

1527
01:04:49.150 --> 01:04:54.910
Dwight is watching Angela and Katie through the window and he is going to get up his nerve to go in and ask her out.
德怀特正透过窗户看着安吉拉和凯蒂，他正鼓起勇气准备进去约她。

1528
01:04:55.010 --> 01:04:57.050
But she turns him down.
但她拒绝了他。

1529
01:04:57.210 --> 01:04:58.010
She's pretty harsh.
她拒绝得挺狠的。

1530
01:04:58.430 --> 01:05:01.230
I was like, oh, made me sad.
我当时就觉得，噢，让我挺难过的。

1531
01:05:01.750 --> 01:05:04.150
We are now going to have a Dwight talking head.
我们现在要看一段德怀特的访谈。

1532
01:05:04.330 --> 01:05:05.990
It's a pretty famous Dwight talking head.
这是一段非常出名的德怀特访谈。

1533
01:05:06.170 --> 01:05:09.350
He outlines what his idea of a perfect date is.
他概述了他心目中完美约会的样子。

1534
01:05:09.830 --> 01:05:10.490
Yes, of course.
是的，当然。

1535
01:05:10.630 --> 01:05:11.270
There's ninjas.
有忍者。

1536
01:05:11.470 --> 01:05:12.010
There's knives.
有刀具。

1537
01:05:12.190 --> 01:05:12.790
There's blood.
有鲜血。

1538
01:05:13.510 --> 01:05:14.390
There's poison.
有毒药。

1539
01:05:14.870 --> 01:05:16.890
But he knew about it all along, guys.
但伙计们，他其实早就知道了。

1540
01:05:17.090 --> 01:05:18.550
She was in on it all along.
她从一开始就参与其中。

1541
01:05:19.470 --> 01:05:20.430
But he knew.
但他知道。

1542
01:05:20.790 --> 01:05:21.450
Oh, right.
噢，对。

1543
01:05:21.770 --> 01:05:23.290
He knew she was in on it.
他知道她参与其中。

1544
01:05:23.350 --> 01:05:23.810
That's right.
没错。

1545
01:05:24.570 --> 01:05:26.890
Luann crosses twice in the background of this talking head.
在这段访谈的背景里，卢安走过了两次。

1546
01:05:27.090 --> 01:05:27.750
Creed crosses.
克里德走过了。

1547
01:05:28.150 --> 01:05:28.410
Devin.
德文也走过了。

1548
01:05:28.570 --> 01:05:29.850
Then at the end, Creed again.
最后，克里德又走了一次。

1549
01:05:30.830 --> 01:05:33.130
I was just like, there's so much crossing.
我当时就想，怎么这么多人走来走去。

1550
01:05:33.650 --> 01:05:41.550
Also, what's really hilarious is that both Creed and Luann cross into the accounting nook by your desk, Angela,
而且，最搞笑的是，克里德和卢安都走进了你办公桌旁边的会计隔间，安吉拉。

1551
01:05:41.790 --> 01:05:46.150
which means that they would cross there and just stand there and then come out.
这意味着他们会走过去，站在那儿，然后出来。

1552
01:05:46.350 --> 01:05:46.890
And cross right back.
然后再走回来。

1553
01:05:46.970 --> 01:05:47.470
But where do they?
但他们去哪儿了？

1554
01:05:47.550 --> 01:05:49.250
They must have just been standing in the corner.
他们肯定刚才一直站在角落里。

1555
01:05:49.470 --> 01:05:50.910
I don't know why they're crossing to accounting.
我不知道他们为什么要穿过会计部。

1556
01:05:50.910 --> 01:05:52.010
I'm in the conference room.
我在会议室里。

1557
01:05:52.110 --> 01:05:53.730
You're with Katie trying to buy a purse.
你正和凯蒂在一起，想买个包。

1558
01:05:53.910 --> 01:05:54.110
Yeah.
是啊。

1559
01:05:54.110 --> 01:05:55.910
What are they doing at your desk?
他们在你桌子旁干什么？

1560
01:05:56.030 --> 01:05:57.410
They're messing with your stuff, Ann.
他们在乱动你的东西，安。

1561
01:05:57.670 --> 01:05:58.210
They're snooping around.
他们在到处窥探。

1562
01:05:59.230 --> 01:05:59.790
Oh, dear.
噢，天哪。

1563
01:06:00.110 --> 01:06:03.910
Now Michael is going to ask Ryan for some help cleaning out his car.
现在迈克尔要找瑞安帮忙清理他的车了。

1564
01:06:04.110 --> 01:06:05.430
This is one of my favorite scenes.
这是我最喜欢的场景之一。

1565
01:06:05.430 --> 01:06:08.050
It's one of my favorite scenes of the whole series.
这是整部剧里我最喜欢的场景之一。

1566
01:06:08.390 --> 01:06:09.130
Blue BlaSt.
蓝色冲击。

1567
01:06:09.190 --> 01:06:10.050
Blue BlaSt.
蓝色冲击。

1568
01:06:10.530 --> 01:06:11.850
Blue is not a favorite.
蓝色不是最喜欢的。

1569
01:06:12.410 --> 01:06:12.850
No.
不是。

1570
01:06:13.050 --> 01:06:13.690
All of it.
全部都是。

1571
01:06:13.830 --> 01:06:16.950
Oh, and he wants the Arctic Blast and the passenger side cup holder.
噢，他还想要北极冲击口味的，还有副驾驶座的杯架。

1572
01:06:17.330 --> 01:06:17.590
Yeah.
是啊。

1573
01:06:17.590 --> 01:06:18.590
That's ready for you, Katie.
凯蒂，那个给你准备好了。

1574
01:06:18.810 --> 01:06:20.030
This is what you're missing.
这就是你错过的东西。

1575
01:06:20.290 --> 01:06:20.730
I know.
我知道。

1576
01:06:20.730 --> 01:06:22.190
You don't get the convertible.
你没得到敞篷车。

1577
01:06:22.190 --> 01:06:24.030
You don't get the Arctic BlaSt.
你没得到北极冲击。

1578
01:06:24.210 --> 01:06:25.810
You don't get the coffee maker.
你没得到咖啡机。

1579
01:06:26.450 --> 01:06:29.090
25 minutes and 8 seconds.
25分8秒。

1580
01:06:29.410 --> 01:06:32.690
Fakie water bottle label and then Fakie Blue Blast label.
伪造的水瓶标签，然后是伪造的蓝色冲击标签。

1581
01:06:33.110 --> 01:06:34.170
Fakie labels.
伪造标签。

1582
01:06:34.410 --> 01:06:35.190
Fakie labels.
伪造标签。

1583
01:06:35.430 --> 01:06:36.310
She's tracking it.
她在追踪这个。

1584
01:06:36.410 --> 01:06:38.370
She's tracking that and who's crossing where.
她在追踪那个，还有谁穿过了哪里。

1585
01:06:38.710 --> 01:06:39.290
I am.
我是在追踪。

1586
01:06:40.010 --> 01:06:43.190
Well, now Jim is going to go into the conference room.
好吧，现在吉姆要进会议室了。

1587
01:06:43.230 --> 01:06:45.430
And what is smooth operator?
那“老练的操盘手”是什么意思？

1588
01:06:45.850 --> 01:06:46.170
Okay.
好的。

1589
01:06:46.170 --> 01:06:47.150
Jenna F.
来自洛杉矶的珍娜·F想知道，这其中有多少是即兴发挥的？

1590
01:06:47.310 --> 01:06:51.010
from Los Angeles wants to know, how much of this was improv?
噢，我会告诉你的。

1591
01:06:51.650 --> 01:06:53.070
Oh, I will tell you.
根据拍摄剧本，这是写好的内容。

1592
01:06:53.470 --> 01:06:56.130
Per the shooting draft, this is what was scripted.
吉姆走向凯蒂。

1593
01:06:56.790 --> 01:06:57.870
Jim approaches Katie.
剧本上说他悄悄走到她身边。

1594
01:06:58.290 --> 01:07:00.350
It says he sidles up to her.
他说，嗨，我是吉姆。

1595
01:07:00.510 --> 01:07:01.890
He says, hi, I'm Jim.
凯蒂说，嗨。

1596
01:07:02.270 --> 01:07:03.170
Katie says, hi.
剩下的都是即兴发挥。

1597
01:07:03.770 --> 01:07:05.270
The rest is improv.
什么？

1598
01:07:05.750 --> 01:07:06.190
What?
剩下的都是即兴发挥，直到他说“别试着向我推销任何东西”那部分。

1599
01:07:06.470 --> 01:07:10.790
The rest is improv until it gets to the part where he says, don't try to sell me anything.
我只是想学习一下。

1600
01:07:10.790 --> 01:07:11.810
I just want to learn.
我只是想学习一下。

1601
01:07:12.310 --> 01:07:13.450
Everything else is improv.
其他一切都是即兴发挥。

1602
01:07:13.670 --> 01:07:14.230
This is improv.
这才是即兴表演。

1603
01:07:14.530 --> 01:07:15.270
I'm Katie.
我是凯蒂。

1604
01:07:15.270 --> 01:07:16.010
Well, hi, Katie.
你好啊，凯蒂。

1605
01:07:16.150 --> 01:07:16.830
Nice to meet you.
很高兴见到你。

1606
01:07:17.030 --> 01:07:18.470
You sit out there, don't you?
你平时都坐在外面，对吧？

1607
01:07:18.610 --> 01:07:18.970
I do.
是的。

1608
01:07:19.090 --> 01:07:20.990
It's what I'm best known for, sitting out there.
坐在外面是我最出名的标签了。

1609
01:07:21.390 --> 01:07:21.890
All right.
好吧。

1610
01:07:22.010 --> 01:07:23.190
Let's talk about purses.
我们来聊聊钱包吧。

1611
01:07:23.370 --> 01:07:24.530
But just talk to me.
但你得跟我聊。

1612
01:07:25.330 --> 01:07:25.770
Seriously.
说真的。

1613
01:07:26.370 --> 01:07:27.670
That was all improvised.
那全都是即兴发挥的。

1614
01:07:28.150 --> 01:07:28.490
Wow.
哇。

1615
01:07:28.690 --> 01:07:29.070
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1616
